    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** headlining the offensive unit. Boasting a stellar 66.18 score, **Kyle Tucker** remains our primary anchor despite the lack of a defined opponent, providing the highest ceiling on the roster. Behind him, **Jackson Merrill** (51.99) earns a high-leverage start against Jacob Misiorowski. While the matchup against a high-pedigree arm like Misiorowski depresses the score slightly, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong dynamic platoon advantage and a premium #4 spot in the lineup, making him a reliable play for counting stats. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (50.07) also clears our 50-point threshold, utilizing a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Drew Rasmussen to offset the difficulty of facing a high-skill arm.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility spot and the remainder of the lineup was tightly contested, particularly regarding our bench depth. **Brayan Rocchio** (34.60) was the closest candidate to cracking the lineup, but he fell well short of our 40-point efficiency floor due to an unfavorable #9 spot in the order and a tough matchup against H. Smith. The optimizer favored **Andy Pages** (53.48) in the utility slot; although batting #7, his raw output projection remains significantly more stable than the alternatives. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Liam Hicks** (40.84) and **Heliot Ramos** (40.99), both of whom are hovering just above the \"Below Floor\" category. Should official lineups shift **Liam Hicks** or **Heliot Ramos** down in the order, we may need to pivot to preserve game caps, as their current efficiency scores are heavily contingent on their assumed cleanup and #3 spots, respectively.",
